# Codex PLAN review — P9C typed app_set_tweak (disclaude). See "## PR P9C" in disclaude.md.

app_set_tweak (builtin/appkit.py:211, currently _coerce_scalar+with_tweak, untyped) becomes governed: validate
the value against the app's TweakSpec (.disco/tweaks.json via tweaks_io.require_tweakspec + spec.validate_value)
before mutating the AppSpec. CONTRACT CHANGE: the tool now REQUIRES a TweakSpec; no tweaks.json → error
no_tweakspec. Errors: no_tweakspec / corrupt_tweakspec / unknown_tweak / invalid_tweak_value, each a clear
ToolOutcome(success=False). On success, persist via _apply(with_tweak(key, coerced)) and echo {tweak, value,
affects} in structured. Validation happens BEFORE the appspec is touched (a bad tweak never mutates the app).

Judge: (a) is making app_set_tweak require a TweakSpec the right call (governance / no-false-affordance) vs a
softer fallback to the old untyped behavior when no tweaks.json exists? (b) is the validate-before-_apply ordering
+ the error taxonomy (no_tweakspec/corrupt_tweakspec/unknown_tweak/invalid_tweak_value) correct + complete? (c)
echoing affects (AppSpec paths) in structured — useful + safe? (d) the open question: WHO writes .disco/tweaks.json
(app_create defaults? a builder? a P9D seed?) — is deferring that out of P9C acceptable, given app_set_tweak is
unusable until something authors the spec? (e) any risk the contract change breaks existing app_set_tweak tests /
the build agent's tool flow, and how to migrate? (f) scope. Return APPROVE|REVISE|BLOCKED + REASONS +
REQUIRED_REVISIONS.
