codex
There’s no current author of `.disco/tweaks.json` in `app_create` or the `lead_form` starter. So the strict contract is coherent, but P9C creates a temporary product gap unless the PR also changes how the tool is advertised or lands with a minimal seed path.
codex
REVISE

**REASONS**
- **(a) Strict TweakSpec requirement is the right call.** Falling back to untyped `with_tweak` would preserve the exact false affordance P9 is trying to remove. `AppSpec.tweaks` is just a value bag; `.disco/tweaks.json` is the governing definition.
- **(b) Validate-before-mutate is correct.** Unknown/invalid values must fail before `AppSpec.with_tweak`. The tweak-specific taxonomy is good, but not complete as a full tool taxonomy: `app_set_tweak` can still return inherited `no_app` / `corrupt_appspec` from `_apply`, and write/backend failures can still surface via executor errors.
- **(c) Echoing `affects` is useful and safe enough** if it is treated as declared AppSpec metadata only. P9A validates it as lexical dotted paths, but it is not proof those paths exist or changed. Echo canonical `value`, not raw input.
- **(d) Deferring the writer is only conditionally acceptable.** Right now `app_create` / `lead_form` starter do not write `.disco/tweaks.json`, while the build prompt advertises `app_set_tweak`. That makes the tool unusable in normal appkit flow until P9D/seed work lands.
- **(e) Existing tests and model flow will break.** `test_set_design_and_tweak` and `test_tweak_coercion_is_robust` currently assume arbitrary untyped keys after `app_create`. The build agent may also keep calling the advertised tool and get `no_tweakspec`.
- **(f) Scope is mostly right**, but the migration/advertising gap must be handled in P9C or explicitly gated.

**REQUIRED_REVISIONS**
- Document the full error contract: tweak errors plus existing `no_app` / `corrupt_appspec` / executor failures. Decide precedence for empty workspace; I recommend preserving `no_app` as the clearer first failure when no app exists.
- Update the tool description/prompt pack to say `app_set_tweak` requires `.disco/tweaks.json`, or stop advertising it to flows that cannot have a TweakSpec yet.
- Either seed a minimal real TweakSpec in `app_create`/starter as part of P9C, or explicitly mark P9C as not product-live until the P9D/builder seed lands.
- Update tests: write a TweakSpec fixture before success cases, convert arbitrary-key coercion tests into `unknown_tweak` / typed validation tests, and assert AppSpec bytes are unchanged on `no_tweakspec`, `corrupt_tweakspec`, `unknown_tweak`, and `invalid_tweak_value`.
- On success, merge `_apply` structured data with `{"tweak": key, "value": coerced, "affects": list(field.affects)}` using a new/model-copied `ToolOutcome`.
